# HAND-OFF FOR A PERSON AT THE PHYSICAL KEYBOARD. Not run by automation; completion of the
# scripted half proves nothing about the IME. Modelled on cue_ime_linux.scn.
#
# BLOCKED ON A MISSING CONTROL: on current Turnstone main the Settings pane has no
# text-entry row (rows are toggle, choice and number controls; the theme workshop is a
# separate window). The `role:textbox` steps below name the control a future Settings text
# row would publish; until one exists this scenario stops at the first assert with
# "no matching node". Set SETTINGS_TEXT_ROW to its accessible name.
#
# What the person does (exchange directory CUE_IME_EXCHANGE, empty, writable):
#   1. When ${CUE_IME_EXCHANGE}/01.ready appears, the Settings text row is focused and empty.
#      With a macOS input method (for example Japanese Hiragana or Pinyin) begin a
#      composition and leave the candidate window OPEN. Do not commit it.
#   2. Create ${CUE_IME_EXCHANGE}/01.sample. The scenario floats and tears the pane out
#      while the candidate is open (decision D4: the host commits, then moves).
#   3. When 02.ready appears, note what the pane shows, then create 02.done. The scenario
#      asserts the committed text is present exactly once in the torn-out window's row.
# Set COMMITTED_TEXT to the exact string the composition commits.
settle 20
key escape
resize 1180 950
open mere://settings-reactive
settle 10
act id:pane:settings
settle 5
assert pane turnstone.settings
click surface:settings role:textbox ${SETTINGS_TEXT_ROW}
settle 3
capture 01_text_row_ready
touch ${CUE_IME_EXCHANGE}/01.ready
wait-file 60000 ${CUE_IME_EXCHANGE}/01.sample
capture 01_text_row_composing
act Float pane
settle 5
act Tear out pane
settle 10
assert windows == 2
assert lens-pane turnstone.settings
touch ${CUE_IME_EXCHANGE}/02.ready
wait-file 60000 ${CUE_IME_EXCHANGE}/02.done
capture-lens 02_torn_out_after
assert node window:1 role:textbox ${SETTINGS_TEXT_ROW} = ${COMMITTED_TEXT}
log Physical IME hand-off collected; the person's observations, not this log, qualify it
